# SussIt Engineering Rules

SussIt is an Australian mobile-first second-hand buying app.

**Strategy source of truth:** `docs/strategy.md` (locked Jul 2026).

**Positioning:** Before I buy anything off Marketplace, I SussIt.

**Free consumer:** “Should I buy this?” / “Know what to pay before you buy.” — screenshot or paste.

**Flip / Pro / Hunter:** later. Do **not** build paywall, Hunter alerts, inventory CRM, or Facebook scraping unless explicitly requested. Next milestone is accuracy + ~20–50 real flippers + ground-truth outcomes.

Core principle:

AI identifies and explains.
Deterministic application code determines prices, Max Buy, scores and confidence.

Never allow an LLM to invent or calculate the fundamental valuation or Max Buy.

## Intelligence tiers

- **full:** phone, console, vr_headset — strong Buy/Offer allowed
- **emerging:** camera, laptop, tablet, wearable, audio, gpu, power_tool — limited framing
- **basic:** furniture, clothing, vehicles, etc. — LIMITED MARKET DATA only

Universal intake; narrow high-confidence verdicts. See `docs/intelligence-tiers.md`.

## Obsess over

% of recommendations users later mark correct — not registrations or scans.

Capture ground truth when possible: contact → buy → purchase price → resell → resale price → time to resale.

## Design

Use /docs/design as the visual source of truth.

Brand:
- #C6FF00 acid lime
- #111111 almost black (phone canvas)
- #FAF8F5 cream (outer page + text)
- #1A1A1A dark surface / #222 panel
- #888888 muted text
- Fonts: Barlow (display), Inter (body)
- UI source of truth: docs/design/prototype/App.tsx

Avoid: gradients, glassmorphism, excessive shadows, generic SaaS, AI sparkles, cluttered dashboards.

## Technical stack

- React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, Supabase, Vercel, OpenAI
- eBay Browse for current AU asking comps (not solds until Insights)

## Architecture

Core valuation: `src/lib/valuation/`
Intelligence tiers / product graph: `src/lib/intelligence/`
Pricing sources implement `PricingProvider` — never couple valuation directly to eBay.

## Product philosophy

Trust > fake precision.

When data is insufficient, return INSUFFICIENT DATA / LIMITED MARKET DATA.

Never fabricate accessories, variants, condition, market prices, seller claims, confidence, or days-to-sell.

Unknown values remain null.

Do not claim sold averages until Marketplace Insights or user-confirmed sales backs them.

Do not add features that were not requested.
